<th id="S7.T11.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><math id="S7.T11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.T11.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> 1e-5</span></th>
<td id="S7.T11.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">56.41</span></td>
<td id="S7.T11.5.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.7.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39.13</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T11.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T11.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><math id="S7.T11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.T11.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> 4e-5 (ours)</span></th>
<td id="S7.T11.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">55.07</span></td>
<td id="S7.T11.5.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">40.84</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T11.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T11.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><math id="S7.T11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.T11.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> 7e-5</span></th>
<td id="S7.T11.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">54.37</span></td>
<td id="S7.T11.5.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.9.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">40.35</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T11.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T11.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><math id="S7.T11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.T11.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> 1e-4 (original)</span></th>
<td id="S7.T11.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">53.91</span></td>
<td id="S7.T11.5.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-0.45pt;padding-bottom:-0.45pt;"><span id="S7.T11.5.10.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39.70</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Interpretation of Hyperparameter <math id="S8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is introduced in the main paper as a temperature-scaling ratio on the calibrated target distribution, it also admits an equivalent similarity/logit-scaling interpretation. Specifically, the calibrated target distribution can be written as</p>
<table id="S8.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}p_{{rob}}^{i,j}&amp;=\frac{\exp\left(\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{j})\right)/(\tau/\gamma)\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{k})\right)/(\tau/\gamma)\right)},\\
&amp;=\frac{\exp\left(\gamma\cdot\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{j})\right)/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(\gamma\cdot\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{k})\right)/\tau\right)}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}p_{{rob}}^{i,j}&amp;=\frac{\exp\left(\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{j})\right)/(\tau/\gamma)\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{k})\right)/(\tau/\gamma)\right)},\\
&amp;=\frac{\exp\left(\gamma\cdot\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{j})\right)/\tau\right)}{\sum_{k}\exp\left(\gamma\cdot\cos\left(f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x^{i}),f_{\phi}(t^{k})\right)/\tau\right)}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, temperature scaling in the distribution space is equivalent to uniformly scaling the original similarities/logits before the softmax. In this section, we use this equivalent similarity-scaling view to provide an intuitive interpretation of the role of <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Given an image <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and a text <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, let
<math id="S8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the pre-trained visual feature,
<math id="S8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the robust visual feature,
and <math id="S8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\phi}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\phi}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> be the text feature.
We <math id="S8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-normalize these features as</p>
<table id="S8.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S8.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{{orig}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{{orig}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)}/{\|f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)\|_{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)}/{\|f_{\theta_{{orig}}}(x)\|_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.E12Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{{rob}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{{rob}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)}/{\|f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)\|_{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)}/{\|f_{\theta_{{rob}}}(x)\|_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.E12Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E12Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={f_{\phi}(t)}/{\|f_{\phi}(t)\|_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={f_{\phi}(t)}/{\|f_{\phi}(t)\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The normalized features satisfy:</p>
<table id="S8.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S8.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cos(f_{\theta_{orig}}(x),f_{\phi}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cos(f_{\theta_{orig}}(x),f_{\phi}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cos(f_{\theta_{rob}}(x),f_{\phi}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cos(f_{\theta_{rob}}(x),f_{\phi}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.5" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\alpha_{orig}-\alpha_{rob}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\alpha_{orig}-\alpha_{rob}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then:</p>
<table id="S8.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}={\langle\delta,\beta\rangle}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}={\langle\delta,\beta\rangle}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.6" class="ltx_p">According to the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality, we have:</p>
<table id="S8.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}|{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}|&amp;=|{\langle\delta,\beta\rangle}|\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}\cdot{\|\beta\|}_{2}={\|\delta\|}_{2}\\
|{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}|&amp;\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}|{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}|&amp;=|{\langle\delta,\beta\rangle}|\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}\cdot{\|\beta\|}_{2}={\|\delta\|}_{2}\\
|{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}|&amp;\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Temperature scaling softens the pre-trained distribution by reducing the effective logit scale. For semantically aligned prompts, the original similarity is typically positive, and adversarial fine-tuning often reduces its magnitude. We therefore consider the common case <math id="S8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}\leq{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}\leq{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives</p>
<table id="S8.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}&amp;\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}\\
1-\frac{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}&amp;\leq\frac{{\|\delta\|}_{2}}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}\\
\rho=\frac{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}&amp;\geq 1-\frac{{\|\delta\|}_{2}}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}-{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}&amp;\leq{\|\delta\|}_{2}\\
1-\frac{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}&amp;\leq\frac{{\|\delta\|}_{2}}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}\\
\rho=\frac{\langle\alpha_{rob},\beta\rangle}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}&amp;\geq 1-\frac{{\|\delta\|}_{2}}{\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S8.E16" title="In 8 Interpretation of Hyperparameter 𝛾 ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> lower-bounds the local similarity contraction factor <math id="S8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the representation shift <math id="S8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: a larger shift leads to a smaller lower bound on <math id="S8.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Other sign configurations yield analogous upper or lower bounds for <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. In zero-shot vision-language classification, however, prediction is mainly determined by semantically aligned prompts with high positive similarity (<math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\alpha_{orig},\beta\rangle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>). Moreover, as shown in <a href="#S4.T9" title="In 4.4 More Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, adversarial fine-tuning typically reduces the absolute scale of these peak cross-modal similarities. Therefore, the positive-similarity degradation case in <a href="#S8.E16" title="In 8 Interpretation of Hyperparameter 𝛾 ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> captures the dominant effect of representation shift.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The local factor <math id="S8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is distinct from the global hyperparameter <math id="S8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> used in AGFT. Rather, <math id="S8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as a global approximation to the dominant contraction behavior over semantically aligned prompts, yielding a softer target distribution that matches the robust model. This discussion provides an intuitive explanation for why temperature calibration helps, rather than formally deriving the optimal <math id="S8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Additional Results</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional experimental results that complement those reported in the main text, including detailed robust accuracy on all 15 datasets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness against Stronger Attacks.</span>
We report robust accuracy under the C&amp;W attack and AutoAttack. The detailed results are presented in <a href="#S10.T12" title="In 10 Future Work ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#S10.T13" title="In 10 Future Work ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-tuning in Diverse Architectures.</span>
We further report robust accuracy for two additional CLIP backbones, namely ViT-B/16 and RN50<math id="S9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>4. The corresponding results are shown in <a href="#S10.T14" title="In 10 Future Work ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and <a href="#S10.T15" title="In 10 Future Work ‣ AGFT: Alignment-Guided Fine-Tuning for Zero-Shot Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10 </span>Future Work</h2>

<div id="S10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although AGFT demonstrates strong performance in improving the zero-shot adversarial robustness of vision-language models, our current evaluation is mainly focused on zero-shot image classification under the <math id="S10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> threat model. In future work, we envision expanding the proposed alignment-guided paradigm along three directions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we will evaluate AGFT under a broader range of threat models, including <math id="S10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-bounded perturbations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, text-level attacks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, and joint text-image attacks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>. Second, we aim to generalize AGFT to a wider variety of model architectures, extending beyond CLIP to other cross-modal models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> and transformer-based architectures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. Finally, we intend to apply AGFT to a broader set of downstream multimodal tasks, such as visual question answering and image captioning, thereby contributing to the development of more secure and trustworthy foundation models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S10.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S10.T12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 12</span>: </span><span id="S10.T12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Zero-shot robust accuracy (%).
Adversarial examples are generated by <span id="S10.T12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C&amp;W</span> attack with
the perturbation budget <math id="S10.T12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/255</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
